Usage: xllama-cli -m <model.gguf> -p <prompt> [options]

Required:
  -m, --model <path>   Path to GGUF model file
  -p, --prompt <text>  Prompt text

Optional:
  -n, --n-predict <N>  Max tokens to generate (default: 128)
  -c, --ctx <N>        Context size (default: 2048)
  -t, --threads <N>    Thread count; 0 = auto (default: 0)
      --temp <float>   Sampling temperature (default: 0.8)
      --seed <int>     RNG seed; 0 = random (default: 0)
      --top-p <float>  Nucleus sampling cutoff (default: 0.9)
      --top-k <N>      Top-k cutoff (default: 40)
      --repetition-penalty <float>
                       Repetition penalty over the last 64 tokens
                       (default: 1.1); 0 disables the stage
      --system <text>  System message for --chat (default: the built-in
                       "You are a helpful AI assistant.")
      --chat           Wrap the prompt with the model's chat template
                       (ChatML, Gemma, Llama 3 or Phi 3 by model name;
                       Qwen no-think suffix) and stop on its stop token
      --batch <N>      Logical prefill batch; 0 = llama default 2048
      --ubatch <N>     Physical prefill chunk (TTFT sweep knob);
                       0 = llama default 512
      --kv-q8          q8_0 KV cache + flash attention (#171); falls
                       back to F16 KV if the arch refuses flash attn
      --prompt-lookup  Draft-free n-gram speculative decoding (GGUF;
                       Phase 15 W2 #210). Default off; host timings are
                       not product claims — console A/B decides ship
      --membw          Run the CPU memory-bandwidth micro-bench and
                       exit (no model needed); prints read/copy/triad GB/s
      --diskbw         Run the disk read-bandwidth micro-bench and exit
                       (no model needed); seq+rnd read GB/s, 4 GiB test file
      --gpubw          Phase 15 W3 (#211) GPU STREAM probe (D3D12; host
